---
name: xf-template-phrase
description: Build or review XenForo templates, template modifications, phrases, LESS, forms, components, and first-party-quality public or admin UI.
---

# XenForo Templates and UI

Load `xf-shared-policy` and `xf-environment`.

XenForo templates use a custom compiled language. They are not Blade, Twig, PHP, or JSX. Similar-looking syntax does not make constructs from those languages valid.

XenForo ships Font Awesome 5 Pro. Use only icon names and weights present in that version; verify uncertain icons against first-party usage or `styles/fa/`.

## Start with the Existing Design System

1. Find comparable first-party pages in `src/addons/XF/_output/templates/public` or `admin`. Use first-party `src/addons/XF*` examples when the feature belongs to another official product.
2. Reuse the established structural component, form row, macro, CSS class, responsive utility, and JavaScript behavior before adding markup or LESS.
3. Use `xf-make:template` and `xf-make:phrase` for new artifacts.
4. Keep authorization, queries, and domain decisions out of templates. Prepare view data in PHP.
5. Verify the rendered result at narrow and wide widths, including empty, error, disabled, and long-content states that the change affects.

Read [template-language-semantics.md](references/template-language-semantics.md) before writing expressions or macros. Read [ui-patterns.md](references/ui-patterns.md) before creating or restyling a form, list, menu, overlay, or content block.

## Filesystem and Database

After manually editing existing `_output/templates` or `_output/phrases` files, run the type-specific importer scoped to the owner:

```text
xf xf-dev:import-templates --addon=Vendor/AddOn
xf xf-dev:import-phrases --addon=Vendor/AddOn
```

Do not run an export, edit `_metadata.json`, or touch `_data` XML. A new make command already synchronized both representations and needs no import.

Read [template-phrase-checklist.md](references/template-phrase-checklist.md) before finalizing.
